## OUTPUT FORMAT & STRUCTURE RULES

[fmt-00003] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: [fmt-00001] :: When a table requires complex content, use HTML-style line breaks (<br>•) or explicit list markers within cells to ensure bulleted lists are rendered correctly. For APA citations, strictly use the format: Author, A. A. (Year). Title. Journal Name.
[fmt-00006] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: [fmt-00004] :: For complex technical specifications or BOMs, adopt a 'Data-First' structure: define a master table with all required columns (Item, Qty, Unit Price, Extended Total, Spec/Link) before drafting prose. For visual requirements, use ASCII art or structured text blocks labeled as 'Figure [N]: [Name]' to ensure all required labels are explicitly present.
[fmt-00008] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: For multi-page document requests, explicitly structure the response with headers for 'Appendix', 'Glossary', and 'Detailed Process Flow'. Use a table for 'Approval Matrices' to map every stakeholder (e.g., Finance, Quality, ER, Purchase, Program Manager) to every gate (e.g., TRAR, Nomination, Delta-Change) to ensure all rubric items are addressed.
## TOOL & API USAGE

## FORMULAS & CALCULATIONS

[calc-00001] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: For audit sample size (n) with a known population (N), use the Finite Population Correction (FPC) formula: n = [Z^2 * p * (1-p) / e^2] / [1 + (Z^2 * p * (1-p) / (e^2 * N))]. Always wrap variance calculations in IFERROR or IF(Q2=0, 'NA', ...) to prevent #DIV/0! errors.
